[%# The syslog listener for the fleet.  Provisioner::Recipe::logcollector has the
    reasoning; the two things worth knowing from in here:

    The input has a ruleset of its own, so what arrives from the network is
    written once, to the file named for its sender, and never reaches the
    default rules.  That is what keeps this guest own /var/log/syslog its own,
    and what confines the stop below to remote messages -- an unscoped one would
    swallow this guest local logging as well.

    secpath-replace is not decoration.  HOSTNAME is whatever the sender put in
    the message, so without it a sender could call itself ../../etc/cron.d/oops
    and choose where this guest writes. -%]
[% IF protocol == 'tcp' || protocol == 'both' -%]
module(load="imtcp")
input(type="imtcp" port="[% port %]" ruleset="logcollector")
[% END -%]
[% IF protocol == 'udp' || protocol == 'both' -%]
module(load="imudp")
input(type="imudp" port="[% port %]" ruleset="logcollector")
[% END -%]
[% FOR sender IN allowed_senders -%]
$AllowedSender TCP, [% sender %]
$AllowedSender UDP, [% sender %]
[% END -%]

template(name="logcollector-perhost" type="string" string="[% log_dir %]/%HOSTNAME:::secpath-replace%.log")

ruleset(name="logcollector") {
    action(type="omfile" dynaFile="logcollector-perhost" dirCreateMode="0755" fileCreateMode="0640")
[%# Above the stop, and that is not a matter of taste: stop ends processing for
    the message, so a forward written below it is one that never runs.

    RFC5424 with octet-counted framing because that is what the telegraf syslog
    input parses; the default rsyslog format is RFC3164, which it rejects.
    These go to a consumer on this guest rather than to another collector --
    Provisioner::Recipe::logcollector has the account. -%]
[% FOR dest IN forward -%]
[% parts = dest.split(':') -%]
    action(type="omfwd" target="[% parts.0 %]" port="[% parts.1 %]" protocol="tcp"
           template="RSYSLOG_SyslogProtocol23Format" TCP_Framing="octet-counted"
           action.resumeRetryCount="-1"
           queue.type="linkedList" queue.size="10000")
[% END -%]
    stop
}
